# Effect: Adds an exact calibration-completion decoder. It checks report ID, data group, command, sub-command, controller, module, and Boolean firmware status.
#   It converts firmware status to the driver status values and reads the unaligned little-endian 16-bit error.
#   Adds command arm, consume, and finish helpers under one IRQ-safe spinlock. Arm reinitializes completion before publication. Consume accepts only the pending selectors.
#   Finish makes the lock winner authoritative: it returns a matched handler result, an interrupt error, or `-ETIMEDOUT`, and clears an unmatched pending request.
#   Adds one report builder. It validates the data pointer and length, clears all 64 bytes, uses the four-byte FPS DPI frame, and uses the five-byte device frame otherwise.
#   Adds one sender that accepts only an exact 64-byte HID write, preserves negative transport errors, and maps a positive short write to `-EIO`.
# Why: Malformed calibration input must not update state. Packed firmware fields cannot be read through an aligned native pointer.
#   Firmware has no sequence token. Completion, timeout, and interruption must arbitrate one pending selector pair without a stale completion escaping into the next request.
#   FPS DPI omits the device byte, unlike the other commands. Every report must contain defined padding and must not read a null payload.
#   A nonnegative HID return is not sufficient. Firmware receives one complete fixed-size packet only when all 64 bytes were written.
@@ -330,6 +365,106 @@
